---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Showcase from "../../../components/Showcase.astro";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/react`;

const html = `<span class="sk-tag">
  <span class="sk-tag__label">design</span>
</span>
<span class="sk-tag" data-tone="accent">
  <span class="sk-tag__label">tokens</span>
</span>
<span class="sk-tag" data-tone="success">
  <span class="sk-tag__label">activo</span>
</span>
<span class="sk-tag" data-tone="warning">
  <span class="sk-tag__label">beta</span>
</span>
<span class="sk-tag" data-tone="danger">
  <span class="sk-tag__label">deprecado</span>
</span>
<span class="sk-tag" data-tone="accent">
  <span class="sk-tag__label">react</span>
  <button
    class="sk-button sk-interactive sk-tag__remove"
    type="button"
    data-variant="ghost"
    data-size="sm"
    data-icon-only
    aria-label="Quitar react"
  >
    <span data-sk-icon="close"></span>
  </button>
</span>
<span class="sk-tag">
  <span class="sk-tag__label">frontend</span>
  <button
    class="sk-button sk-interactive sk-tag__remove"
    type="button"
    data-variant="ghost"
    data-size="sm"
    data-icon-only
    aria-label="Quitar frontend"
  >
    <span data-sk-icon="close"></span>
  </button>
</span>`;

const react = `import { Tag } from "@skryensya/react/tag";

<Tag>design</Tag>
<Tag tone="accent">tokens</Tag>
<Tag tone="success">activo</Tag>
<Tag tone="warning">beta</Tag>
<Tag tone="danger">deprecado</Tag>
<Tag
  tone="accent"
  onRemove={() => remove("react")}
  removeLabel="Quitar react"
>
  react
</Tag>
<Tag onRemove={() => remove("frontend")} removeLabel="Quitar frontend">
  frontend
</Tag>;`;
---

<Base title="Tag" description="Tag: optionally removable keyword chip, with tones and React component.">
  <h1>Tag</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Tag classifies content that the user can act on: filters, facets, chips. where
    <a href="/en/components/badge">Badge</a> is a read-only status tag, Tag is more
    square (control radius, not pill) to be read as actionable, and may have a remove button.
  </p>

  <Showcase html={html} react={react} label="Tag" />
  <p>
    When removable, the label and the remove button are two different purposes: the name
    accessible control names the tag it removes.
  </p>

  <h2>The X is a Button, not a drawing of one</h2>
  <p>
    The remove control is an actual <a href="/en/components/button">Button</a> —
    <code>sk-button sk-interactive</code> with <code>data-size="sm"</code>,
    <code>data-icon-only</code> and <code>data-variant="ghost"</code>— and
    <code>sk-tag__remove</code> is just the modifier that shrinks it to the height of the capsule. Tag no
    sends own interaction.
  </p>
  <p>
    What you gain is what you no longer have to maintain here: the hover and the press come from the
    <a href="/en/state-layer">state layer</a>, the focus ring is the same as all controls, and
    the touch area reaches <strong>44px</strong> by the <code>::after</code> of the button although the
    face paint 20px. Before they were 20px for face and 20px for useful white.
  </p>
  <p>
    The color is still <code>currentColor</code>, so each shade brings its X in its own color
    without a rule per tone.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of the preview. <code>onRemove</code> is optional.</p>
</Base>
